  "description": "PAFHEN crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H110 Ce4 Fe4 N10 O30,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Fe1A (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2A (Fe) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.361-3.915 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.96-129.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C59H122Ce4Fe4N10O33. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 tea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
